fast-rdp-server (0.7.2) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Broker: a missing [web] gateway_user no longer crashes the broker (and
    every RDP login with it). It logs an error, refuses the web gateway's
    operations, fails logins in [mfa] mode web at once, and picks the
    account up without a restart once it exists; --check only warns.
  * Docs: Keycloak MFA flow without Ansible (docs/examples/keycloak-mfa:
    kcadm.sh script, admin console JSON, keycloak-config-cli, realm import);
    screenshots of the waiting screen and the web approval pages; status
    table updated.

 -- Marcel Ritter <marcel@linux-ng.de>  Fri, 23 Oct 2026 11:03:10 +0200

fast-rdp-server (0.7.1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Security fixes from the 0.7.0 review: test notifications limited to one
    per user per minute and kept from delaying approvals (bounded queues);
    webpush_extra_hosts match the exact host and UnifiedPush paths only;
    push endpoints re-checked before every send; channel data during the
    desktop picker capped at 4 MiB; approvals always need an MFA proof,
    also with allow_without_mfa_proof; user-controlled values logged
    quoted; ids and user names matched exactly (trailing newline refused).
  * Approval link for one login while other logins of the user wait: red
    warning box with this login's code, warning in the logs.
  * Ansible: _fastrdp-web created before the broker starts (fresh deploys
    with the web gateway); switching fastrdp_web_enabled off removes the
    web stack; nginx, webgate and broker restarted on new certificates and
    CA files; fixes for wlroots-only build mode, NVIDIA driver install,
    first Guacamole start, provider none, check mode and NFS Kerberos homes.
  * Docs: Windows hosts as back-end researched and deferred (backlog B1).

 -- Marcel Ritter <marcel@linux-ng.de>  Thu, 22 Oct 2026 22:33:18 +0200

fast-rdp-server (0.7.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Waiting screen on by default (fastrdp_proxy_waiting_screen and the
    module's [FastRDP] WaitingScreen default) with a new look: antialiased
    Roboto text on a card with rounded corners, countdown bar, QR code tile.
  * The waiting screen's QR code opens the approval for that login
    (<approve_url>?login=<id>); it can be approved although other logins of
    the user wait. [ui] approve_url now at most 184 characters.
  * Web sign-ins that do not prove MFA get a "Second factor required" page
    and an actionable log line; the setup wizard and preflight cover
    Keycloak's MFA for acr=mfa (fastrdp_web_passkeys).
  * Deploy fix: the base role's upgrade handlers use systemctl try-restart
    and no longer fail when a service is not installed yet (identity's
    flush_handlers); handler names unique across roles (the web gateway's
    "Reload nftables" replaced the base role's).
  * Notifications: Android without Google services (ntfy app, UnifiedPush),
    fastrdp_web_notify_webpush_extra_hosts.

 -- Marcel Ritter <marcel@linux-ng.de>  Thu, 22 Oct 2026 21:34:42 +0200

fast-rdp-server (0.6.1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Deploy fix: the web gateway's restart handler (notified by the base
    role's package upgrade on every host) failed on hosts without the web
    gateway ("Could not find the requested service fastrdp-webgate.service");
    it now runs only with fastrdp_web_enabled.
  * Importable Keycloak client for the web gateway
    (docs/examples/keycloak-fastrdp-web-client.json, verified on Keycloak
    26.8.1); make test-keycloak works again with ansible-core 2.21.
  * Setup wizard: clearer second-factor question (web = Keycloak,
    push/otp/otp_or_push = privacyIDEA, push_or_web = both).

 -- Marcel Ritter <marcel@linux-ng.de>  Thu, 22 Oct 2026 18:03:41 +0200

fast-rdp-server (0.6.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Approval notifications for web approval (opt in at /web/notify): ntfy
    (per-user topic) and Web Push (installable web app, iOS 16.4+ from the
    home screen); the notification only links to /web/approve, approving
    still needs the fresh sign-in. Two-digit login code in notifications,
    on the approval page and on the waiting screen. Off by default
    (fastrdp_web_notify_backends).
  * Desktop picker in the RDP waiting screen ([broker] desktop_picker,
    default never): users with more than one allowed desktop choose with
    digits, arrows + Enter or a click; never with a single desktop or a
    client hint; needs the waiting screen. fastrdp-freerdp3 3.32.2-6
    (patches/freerdp/0007: input while the proxy waits for the broker).

 -- Marcel Ritter <marcel@linux-ng.de>  Thu, 22 Oct 2026 17:28:15 +0200

fast-rdp-server (0.5.3) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Includes 0.5.2, which was tagged but never published (a broker test
    assumed a non-root uid and failed in CI, where the tests run as root;
    fixed).
  * Waiting screen during the second factor (proxy [FastRDP] WaitingScreen,
    Ansible fastrdp_proxy_waiting_screen, default off): the RDP window shows
    what to do (push, web approval with URL and QR code, countdown) and
    "Connecting to your desktop…"; texts per language in [ui.<lang>];
    optional Status Info PDUs ([FastRDP] StatusInfo, default off).
  * fastrdp-freerdp3 3.32.2-5: the proxy forwards Server Status Info PDUs
    only to clients that announce support (patches/freerdp/0006).

 -- Marcel Ritter <marcel@linux-ng.de>  Thu, 22 Oct 2026 15:16:59 +0200

fast-rdp-server (0.5.2) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Proxy broker timeout 180 s (was 120): room for the session start after a
    90 s web approval; with web approval the roles require approval timeout
    + 90 <= fastrdp_proxy_broker_timeout (approval capped at 510). Sites that
    set fastrdp_proxy_broker_timeout: 120 explicitly must raise it.
  * fastrdpctl desktop USER [DESKTOP | --clear]: show, set or clear the
    desktop stored from the web gateway, and why a login gets which desktop.
  * .rdp downloads carry audiomode/audiocapturemode from fastrdp_audio and
    fastrdp_audio_input.
  * Setup wizard offers web approval, KDC evidence and the audio switches;
    preflight checks KDC evidence (fastrdp-freerdp3 >= 3.32.2-4, items,
    Samba vs Microsoft AD) and the web approval timeouts.

 -- Marcel Ritter <marcel@linux-ng.de>  Thu, 22 Oct 2026 13:39:37 +0200

fast-rdp-server (0.5.1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Security: back-end TLS certificates pinned (the broker sends each target's
    SHA-256, proxy.ini CertificatePolicy=deny; hand-written proxy.ini files must
    change "allow" to "deny"); missing homes created outside the broker's
    ProtectHome sandbox; FreeIPA join password on stdin; CI signing key only in
    the steps that use it, actions pinned to commit SHAs.
  * MFA web approval ([mfa] mode = web / push_or_web): approve a pending RDP
    login on the web gateway after a fresh Keycloak sign-in (passkeys, Windows
    Hello).
  * MFA from KDC evidence per login ([mfa] kdc_evidence_as_mfa): FreeIPA
    authentication indicators and AD PAC SIDs (S-1-18-3/-4, AMA groups) skip
    the second factor (fastrdp-freerdp3 3.32.2-4).
  * Desktop choice for RDP logins on the web gateway's chooser page, .rdp
    file download.
  * Audio and microphone for xrdp, wlroots and GNOME sessions
    (fastrdp_audio, fastrdp_audio_input).
  * Base role: package check by script, stops if packages stay older than
    the roles; CI deploys GitHub Pages from main and checks the site is live.
  * Docs: MFA options with mstsc, Windows Hello (incl. Samba AD), audio.

 -- Marcel Ritter <marcel@linux-ng.de>  Thu, 22 Oct 2026 12:14:49 +0200

fast-rdp-server (0.5.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Kerberos NLA from Windows mstsc with AD: user-to-user acceptor
    (fastrdp-freerdp3 3.32.2-3), machine account entries in the proxy keytab.
  * Proxy NLA acceptor offers only Kerberos; NTLM attempts logged with a hint.
  * Session TGTs: default-cache checks and kswitch, ticket visibility
    (fastrdpctl status/tickets), per-group session_tgt, expiry reminder in
    sessions (fastrdp_tgt_notify).
  * SMB/CIFS homes via gssproxy (opt-in), KDC proxy on the web gateway (opt-in),
    browser SPNEGO policies and a .deb Firefox option (opt-in).
  * Power actions blocked for users in RDP sessions (polkit rule).
  * CI: publish queue and lease push to gh-pages, Pages deployed by the workflow.

 -- Marcel Ritter <marcel@linux-ng.de>  Wed, 21 Oct 2026 23:01:19 +0200

fast-rdp-server (0.4.4) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Remote Credential Guard (mstsc /remoteGuard): refused with a negotiation
    response instead of a dropped connection (fastrdp-freerdp3 3.32.2-2); new
    opt-in proxy.ini [FastRDP] AcceptRemoteGuard (Ansible
    fastrdp_accept_remote_guard) accepts it identity-only, discarding the
    forwarded Kerberos tickets; the broker gets "remote_guard": true.
  * Deploys also upgrade the vendored FreeRDP/xrdp packages when they are older
    than the checkout's packaging (fastrdp-freerdp3 3.32.2-2).

